<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: ["struct", "substruct", "function_calls", "logical_indexing"],
}
-->

<statement>
	<p>
		Given the car data set and a manufacturer, gather summary information about the manufacturer's cars.
	</p>
	
	<tabular valign="top" halign="right" top="minor">
		<col width="12%"/>
		<col width="88%" halign="left"/>
			<row>
			<cell>Inputs:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>data</pf> (1 x 1) struct — from <pf>'carbig.mat'</pf></p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>feature</pf> (1 x N) char vector — field of <pf>data</pf> (e.g., <pf>'Model'</pf>, <pf>'Weight'</pf>)</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row bottom="minor">
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>value</pf> (1 x 1) double or (1 x M) char vector — the value to match</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell>Outputs:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>index_list</pf> (R x 1) logical vector — <pf>index_list(k)</pf> is <pf>true</pf> if the <pf>feature</pf> is a field of <pf>data</pf> AND equals <pf>value</pf>; <pf>false</pf> otherwise.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
			<cell>Details:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p>Use <pf>numel</pf>, <pf>size</pf>, or <pf>length</pf> to get the number of values in the list.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>Initialize the output variable as a logical vector of all <pf>true</pf> or all <pf>false</pf> values. You may use <pf>true(m,1)</pf> or <pf>false(m,1)</pf> to do this.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>Use a loop to update the default values in the output vector.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>The input <pf>data</pf> is loaded from <pf>'carbig.mat'</pf> (see below).</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row bottom="minor">
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>Use <pf>isfield</pf> to test if a char vector names a field; use <pf>isa</pf> to distinguish text vs numbers.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>

	</tabular>

	<p>
		Examples:
		<program>
			<code>
				car_data = load('carbig.mat');
				mfg_info = get_mfg_info(car_data, 'amc')
				% should return a struct like:
				% manufacturer: 'amc'
				% country: 'USA   '      % note padded spaces
				% number_of_models: 29
				% acceleration: struct with fields min, max, avg (e.g., min 8.5, max 20.5, avg ~15.12)
				% displacement: struct with fields min, max, avg
				% horsepower:   struct with fields min, max, avg
				% mpg:          struct with fields min, max, avg (e.g., min 13, max 27.4, avg ~18.25)
				% weight:       struct with fields min, max, avg
			</code>
		</program>
	</p>
</statement>